Hi all,

I encountered problems accessing standardized summary output when using runMI, as described here: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/lavaan/4FUDQdyniO0

Following the suggested solution, I re-installed semTools and Lavaan using this code:

install.packages("lavaan", repos = "http://www.da.ugent.be", type = "source")
install.packages("devtools")
devtools::install_github("simsem/semTools/semTools")

This solved the standardized output issue, but I'm now unable to access fit indices or use the chi argument.

Using the classic Holzinger & Swineford data, with added missingness:

HS.model <- ' visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3
              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 '

HSMiss <- HolzingerSwineford1939[,paste("x", 1:9, sep="")]
randomMiss <- rbinom(prod(dim(HSMiss)), 1, 0.1)
randomMiss <- matrix(as.logical(randomMiss), nrow=nrow(HSMiss))
HSMiss[randomMiss] <- NA

including the "chi" argument results in an error, regardless of whether cfa.mi or runMI is used:

#MI using semTools
full.out <- cfa.mi(HS.model, data=HSMiss, m = 3, chi="all", seed = 831517)
full2.out <- runMI(HS.model, data=HSMiss, m = 3, chi="all", fun="cfa", seed = 831517)

> full.out <- cfa.mi(HS.model, data=HSMiss, m = 3, chi="all", seed = 831517)
Error in lavaan::lavaan(model = " visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3\n              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6\nspeed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 ",  :
  lavaan ERROR: unknown argument `chi'
> full2.out <- runMI(HS.model, data=HSMiss, m = 3, chi="all", fun="cfa", seed = 831517)
Error in lavaan::lavaan(model = " visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3\n              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6\nspeed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 ",  :
  lavaan ERROR: unknown argument `chi'

The same occurs when data is imputed using mice, then called in a list:

#MI using mice, cfa using semTools
HSimputed <- mice(HSMiss, m = 3, seed = 831517)

nImputations <- 3
HSimp.list <- list()
for (i in 1:nImputations) {
  HSimp.list[[i]] <- mice::complete(HSimputed, action = i)
}

imp.out <- cfa.mi(HS.model, data=HSimp.list, chi="all", seed = 831517 )
imp2.out <- runMI(HS.model, data=HSimp.list, chi="all", fun="cfa", seed = 831517)

> imp.out <- cfa.mi(HS.model, data=HSimp.list, chi="all", seed = 831517 )
Error in lavaan::lavaan(model = " visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3\n              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6\nspeed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 ",  :
  lavaan ERROR: unknown argument `chi'
> imp2.out <- runMI(HS.model, data=HSimp.list, chi="all", fun="cfa", seed = 831517)
Error in lavaan::lavaan(model = " visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3\n              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6\nspeed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 ",  :
  lavaan ERROR: unknown argument `chi'

Finally, when using runMI or cfa.mi without the chi argument, another error occurs:

#fit indicies
fit.out <- cfa.mi(HS.model, data=HSimp.list, seed = 831517 )
inspect(fit.out, "fit")

> fit.out <- cfa.mi(HS.model, data=HSimp.list, seed = 831517 )
> inspect(fit.out, "fit")
Error in lavListInspect(object = object, what = what, add.labels = TRUE,  :
  unknown `what' argument in inspect function: `fit'

I'd be incredibly grateful for any assistance. Thanks.

