> Is there any way to do this? As far as I can tell, lavaan only takes sample sizes as input, not standard errors.

SEs are the the square-roots of diagonal elements of the asymptotic covariance matrix (ACOV) of the estimated parameters.  If you have access to ACOV from the external software that estimated your (co)variance components, you can supply it to lavaan() using the NACOV= argument.  But I think you would still need sample size, because lavaan expects N times the ACOV.

> *A related question - how does lavaan calculated the standard errors of variances of exogenous variables given a covariance matrix as input? The normal approximation of 2sigma^2/(n-1) seems to differ slightly from what lavaan calculates.

>From the second derivative of the maximum likelihood fitting function, or some other closed-form solution for least-squares estimators.  You can find some details here:

http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2013.824793

