Unfortunately it doesn't seem to matter what the value of acov.matrix is - lavaan's estimates of the standard errors remain the same. Am I making a very basic error? I'm not sure what format the ACOV matrix is meant to be in. I couldn't understand the lavaan documentation on this point.

Minimal working example:

library(lavaan)

lower <-'
1
0.02195847    0.106496
0.02449926    0.05205956    0.151877'

cov.matrix <-
  getCov(lower, names = c("Z","M","R"))

acov.matrix.lower <-'
0.067
0.0036    0.00076
0.0051    0.00063    0.0015'

acov.matrix <-
  getCov(acov.matrix.lower, names = c("Z","M","R"))

pathmodel <- 'Z~~varZ*Z
M~bMZ*Z
R~bRZ*Z+bRM*M'

fit <- sem(pathmodel,
                     sample.cov = cov.matrix,
                     NACOV=100*acov.matrix, #changing this does not change the output
