On Monday, February 12, 2018 at 10:50:34 AM UTC-5, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:
> > has the mixture modeling feature been added to the newest version of lavaan?
>
> No, and I don't think it is anywhere near the top of the list of features the developer plans to add.  He is currently putting all his energy into the multilevel functionality.
>
> > Mplus wont allow me to estimate the intercepts.  ... how did lavaan manage to estimate this model?
>
> Nothing magic, lavaan just does not impose that constraint on its model-specification.  There are hacks to do so in Mplus that involve specifying a single-indicator "phantom" construct for each categorical item, whose intercept can then be freed.  There is an example of it in this article:
>
> https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11336-016-9506-0#Sec26
